#+TITLE: Captain's Bridge — org-llm vital signs
#+SUPERSET_DASHBOARD: captains-bridge
#+SUPERSET_DATABASE: org-llm
#+FILETAGS: :template:superset:dashboard:captain:
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil num:nil

# The admin-pulse dashboard owned by =@picard=. Six charts, one per
# vital sign, single-column layout. Every metric expression here is
# verbatim from =org_llm/metrics/registry.yaml= so the dashboard and
# the =@analyst=-style agents agree on numbers byte-for-byte.

* Agent delegation heatmap
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

Total =crew_log= actions from each =agent_from= to each =agent_to= —
the proxy-vs-manager dominance lens. A bright row on =proxy= means
the manager is not earning its keep; a bright row on =@picard= means
delegation is healthy.

(Originally used =agent_fan_out= but that metric is =COUNT(DISTINCT
agent_to)= — degenerate when =agent_to= is also in the group, which
gives every cell =1= and breaks heatmap color-scale legend
computation. =crew_actions= = =COUNT(*)= shows real interaction
volume.)

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name agent_delegation_heatmap :metric crew_actions :group_by [agent_from, agent_to]
SELECT agent_from, agent_to, COUNT(*) AS crew_actions
FROM crew_log
GROUP BY agent_from, agent_to
#+END_SRC

* Model cost & latency
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: bar
:END:

Mean wall-clock duration of LLM calls bucketed by =call_kind= ×
=model=. The 87× chat/embed gap should jump out instantly; new
spikes flag slow models or context-bloat regressions.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name model_cost_latency :metric llm_avg_ms :group_by [call_kind, model]
SELECT call_kind, model, AVG(duration_ms) AS llm_avg_ms
FROM llm_calls
GROUP BY call_kind, model
#+END_SRC

* Model usage by outcome
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: dist_bar
:END:

Total LLM calls per model, stacked by outcome. Bar height surfaces
sample size; segment proportions surface error rate. Solves the
"phi3.5 50% from n=46 looks like mistral 100% from n=2" problem the
flat error-rate bar hid. (Redesigned by =@geordi= 2026-05-07.)

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name model_usage_by_outcome :metric llm_calls :group_by [outcome, model]
SELECT model, outcome, COUNT(*) AS llm_calls
FROM llm_calls
GROUP BY model, outcome
#+END_SRC

* Captain's-log heatmap
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

When activity happens, by category. Rows = =hist_kind= (capture,
chat, agent, …), columns = day. Sparse rows or sudden bands flag
either a quiet day or a runaway agent loop.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name captains_log_heatmap :metric hist_events :group_by [hist_kind, hist_day]
SELECT kind AS hist_kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS hist_day, COUNT(*) AS hist_events
FROM history
GROUP BY kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Memory probe alert pattern
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

Daily alert counts per sensor probe. Heatmap localizes alerts to
specific probes (memory, cpu, battery, …) instead of averaging the
overall alert rate, which hid the spike pattern. (Redesigned by
=@geordi= 2026-05-07: switched from line of =probe_alert_rate= to
heatmap of =sensor_alerts=.)

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name probe_alert_pattern :metric sensor_alerts :group_by [sensor_day, probe]
SELECT date(ts, 'unixepoch') AS sensor_day, probe, SUM(CASE WHEN status IN ('watch','alert','critical') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS sensor_alerts
FROM sensor_log
GROUP BY date(ts, 'unixepoch'), probe
#+END_SRC

* History workload composition
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: area
:END:

Total events per =hist_kind= per day, stacked. Replaces the flat
=COUNT(DISTINCT kind)= line (which always read 3-5) with actual
workload composition — dominant kinds form the baseline, spikes in
specific kinds appear as steep rises. (Redesigned by =@geordi=
2026-05-07: =hist_kind_count= → =hist_events= grouped by both =hist_day=
and =hist_kind=.)

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name history_workload_composition :metric hist_events :group_by [hist_kind, hist_day]
SELECT kind AS hist_kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS hist_day, COUNT(*) AS hist_events
FROM history
GROUP BY kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

# Run:
#   org-llm superset import-org docs/templates/org-llm-captains-bridge.org.example \
#       --emit-only /tmp/captains-bridge.zip
#   org-llm superset import-org docs/templates/org-llm-captains-bridge.org.example \
#       --post http://localhost:8088
